{"abstract":[{"text":"Merges only the rows persistent history says changed, falling back to a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" whenever history can’t answer."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"text":"MainActor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mergeChanges","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"into","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"store","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC","text":"Store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"policy","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV","text":"MergePolicy","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The live store to reconcile.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"store"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Narrows the configured policy for this call only."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"policy"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is what a remote-change observer should call. Where","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" re-reads every row of every registered entity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on every tick, this reads the store’s transaction log since the last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"merge and spends the result through "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"— so a tick on an N-row table where k rows changed costs O(k). A tick with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no transactions behind it costs one history fetch and nothing else."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every guarantee the other two make holds here. Deletions come from history","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tombstones, which are positive evidence, so unlike a full re-hydration this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"can","type":"text"}]},{"text":" remove the last surviving row. Pending local writes and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds still win, and that is not configurable."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"When it re-reads everything instead","anchor":"When-it-re-reads-everything-instead"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The narrow path is an optimisation, never a weakening: anything that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves a window unaccounted for falls back to the full read, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fallback keeps its empty-snapshot guard — which stops it ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"inferring"}]},{"text":" a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deletion from an empty table, never applying one a tombstone already","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"proved. It happens on a tick with no watermark (hydration and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"re-hydration after a container rebuild both leave one), when the watermark has expired or the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"history fetch fails, when a deletion’s tombstone carries no identity","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(every row deleted before ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Attribute(.preserveValueOnDeletion)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shipped),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when a changed row can’t be resolved, and when more than one store sits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"behind the container.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The watermark advances whenever a tick read every registered entity","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"successfully — including a tick that declined to apply some of what it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read. A row an editing hold defers is carried forward by identity and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"re-offered next tick, which is what keeps a hold from quietly becoming a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"veto without costing a full table read per tick to prevent. See"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Both outcomes are reported: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceDiagnostic\/Kind-swift.struct\/remoteChangesMerged"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for a narrowed tick, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceDiagnostic\/Kind-swift.struct\/historyUnavailable"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a reason for a fallback. A narrowed tick counts what it re-offered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"separately from what it merged, so a hold that is never released — which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes every tick re-offer the same rows forever — reads as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceDiagnostic\/carriedOverCount"},{"text":" equal to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceDiagnostic\/mergedCount"},{"text":", rather than as healthy traffic.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeChanges(into:policy:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mergeChanges","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"into","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC","text":"Store","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeId